<!--
  The same mark WITHOUT its shield: the bare globe the VPN section shows while
  this device's own tunnel is down. The shield closes around it when a session
  comes up (`SectionPresentation.icon`), which is how both apps of this family
  say "connected" — the Apple side draws the same two glyphs in its tab bar and
  gryonixVPN in the Mac menu bar.

  **The state is WHICH GLYPH, never a colour.** A tab bar tints its icon for
  selection, so a green "connected" mark would be repainted to nothing.

  Byte for byte the paths of `tab_icon_logo.xml` minus the first one, which is
  the shield — not a redrawing. `BrandMarkParityTest` holds that relationship on
  both platforms, so a globe that stops being the mark's own globe goes red.

  **The canvas is NOT the mark's, and that is the point (2026-09-08).** The
  shield fills the mark's square; the globe inside it fills half of it, so the
  globe on the mark's own canvas drew a picture visibly smaller than every
  symbol standing beside it in the bar — and the section appeared to shrink
  when a session dropped. The canvas is cropped to the globe instead (5668
  rather than 8553, offset 1266), which is the same drawing enlarged by
  8553/5668, and the stroke is divided by exactly that factor — 225, so the
  line comes to the same 0.95 points on screen as the mark's 340 does. Both
  numbers move together or the mark thins when it opens; `TabIconGlobe.svg`
  carries the same pair, and `BrandMarkParityTest` holds them to each other.
-->
